#NEXUS

[ hill2003a_fig9: Slanted cladogram on a spine (classed slanted): under the out-of-scope ruling for slanted cladograms on a spine (otero2010a_fig15), flagged. The Huayangosaurus line and the Scelidosaurus+Emausaurus line converge into one wedge that meets the spine where the root stem leaves it; read as a root polytomy of three. Node N is a polytomy of six (the Tarchia+Saichania pair, four genera and the Euoplocephalus line). Node letters A-P (white dots) are not clade names and are not encoded. 24 tips, 2 polytomies (3, 6 children). Sample 10 case (census 3, seed 20261274). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

BEGIN TAXA;
    DIMENSIONS NTAX=24;
    TAXLABELS
        Huayangosaurus
        Scelidosaurus
        Emausaurus
        Pawpawsaurus
        Silvisaurus
        Sauropelta
        Panoplosaurus
        Edmontonia
        Animantarx
        Gargoyleosaurus
        Gastonia
        Gobisaurus
        Minmi
        Pinacosaurus
        Talarurus
        Shamosaurus
        Tsagantegia
        Tarchia
        Saichania
        Tianzhenosaurus
        Nodocephalosaurus
        Shanxia
        Ankylosaurus
        Euoplocephalus
    ;
END;

BEGIN TREES;
    TREE hill2003a_fig9 = [&R] (Huayangosaurus,(Scelidosaurus,Emausaurus),((Pawpawsaurus,(Silvisaurus,(Sauropelta,(Panoplosaurus,(Edmontonia,Animantarx))))),(Gargoyleosaurus,(Gastonia,(Gobisaurus,(Minmi,(Pinacosaurus,(Talarurus,((Shamosaurus,Tsagantegia),((Tarchia,Saichania),Tianzhenosaurus,Nodocephalosaurus,Shanxia,Ankylosaurus,Euoplocephalus))))))))));
END;
